>Yellin</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Berne</surname><given-names>TV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In vitro activities of nontraditional antimicrobials against multiresistant <italic>Acinetobacter baumannii </italic>strains isolated in an intensive care unit outbreak</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>2000</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>1035</fpage><lpage>1040</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10722508</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AAC.44.4.1035-1040.2000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hancock</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antibiotic uptake into Gram-negative bacteria</article-title><source>Eur J Clin Microbiol Infect Dis</source><year>1988</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>713</fpage><lpage>720</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2850910</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01975036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Clinical Laboratory Standards Institute</collab></person-group><source>Performance Standards for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing: Seventh Informational Supplement M100-S15</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>CLSI, Wayne, Pennsylvania, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gales</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reis</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contemporary Assessment of Antimicrobial Susceptibility testing Methods for Polymyxin B and Colistin: Review of Available Interpretative Criteria and Quality Control Guidelines</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2001</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11136768</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.39.1.183-190.2001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Clinical Laboratory Standards Institute</collab></person-group><source>Performance Standards for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing: Seventh Informational Supplement M100-S17</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>CLSI, Wayne, Pennsylvania, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>British Society for Antimicrobial Chemotherapy</collab></person-group><article-title>BSAC Disc Diffusion Method for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing, Version 4</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.bsac.org.uk/_db/_documents/version_4_january_2005_final_NH_april_2.pdf"/><comment>(28 April 2006, date last accessed)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Comit&#x000e9; de l'Antibiogramme de la Soci&#x000e9;t&#x000e9; Fran&#x000e7;aise de Microbiologie</collab></person-group><article-title>Recommandations du CASFM, Communiqu&#x000e9; 2005 (Edition de Janvier 2005)</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.sfm.asso.fr/doc"/><comment>(28 April 2006, date last accessed).</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Committee for Clinical Laboratory Standards</collab></person-group><article-title>Methods for dilution antimicrobial susceptibility test for bacteria that grow aerobically</article-title><source>Approved standard M7-A5</source><year>2002</year><edition>5</edition><publisher-name>NCCLS, Wayne, Pa</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Package Insert</collab></person-group><source>BD BBL sensi-Disc Antimicrobial SusceptibilityTest Discs</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Maryland, USA: Becton, Dickinson and Company</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Committee for Clinical Laboratory Standards</collab></person-group><article-title>Development of In Vitro Susceptibility Testing Criteria and Quality Control Parameters: Approved Standard</article-title><source>NCCLS M23-A2</source><year>1981</year><publisher-name>NCCLS, Wayne, PA, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderegg</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Swenson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality Control Working Group. Quality control guidelines for testing gram-negative control strains with polymyxin B and colistin (polymyxin E) by standardized methods</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>925</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15695708</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.43.2.925-927.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tenover</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Arbeit</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Goering</surname><given-names>RV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How to select and interpret molecular strain typing methods for epidemiological studies of bacterial infections: a review for healthcare epidemiologists. Molecula